WEBVTT

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.200
Bar-Baral

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.160
Don't make me repeat myself.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.670
Bring her back.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.380
By any means necessary.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.050
Go on, offer the man
a little help.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.550
Or are you telling me that
the overseer of the colonies

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.850
is afraid of some island pirates?

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.390
If it becomes known that soldiers
frequent the island,

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.310
it will no longer be able
to function as a free city.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.560
That would also be less than ideal
for England, financially speaking.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:56.570
Ah, I follow you.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:03.450
So it's not just America's farms that are under
English control, but also the free cities?

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.580
Dearie, dearie...
That's a frightful prospect.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.330
All right. Use them
as you see fit.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.210
I can always count on
your kind assistance, O'Malley.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.890
It sure is cramped in here...

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.560
Is that a complaint
about my design that I hear?

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.640
No! Never!
I wouldn't dream of it!

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:35.980
The drive transmission system uses whale baleen.
For lubricating oil, whale blubber.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.070
Whales are awesome.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.740
- What's the ship's name?
- The <i>Bonito II.</i>

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.650
<i>Bonito</i>? Not <i>Whale?</i>

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.160
Yep. <i>Bonito.</i>

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.030
Why?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.910
'Cause bonito are delicious.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.160
You have a point.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.170
- I brought her!
- Great, let's get to it!

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.210
Hm? Where's Yukimaru?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.050
Probably off making
his usual you-know-what.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.510
We don't need him here.
I don't wanna get whacked again.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.930
- He whacks you too, Karin?!
- He got you too?!

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:07.550
Now I get it... He must have
a problem with beautiful women.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.890
Beautiful women?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.060
Oh, I get it.
We're just too pretty...

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.900
Listen, Yukimaru is ambidextrous,
so this is how you block his attacks.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.900
Okay, I'll fill you all in
on our upcoming plans.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.940
- Like this?
- No! Like this!

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.320
Let's start with
where we're headed.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.940
If our objective is
procuring supplies, we--

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.400
Oo! Question! Question!
Here! Here!

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.450
- Yes, what is it?
- I wanna buy some clothes!

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:28.950
Clothes?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.330
You look fine in that.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:36.710
That's not the point!

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.960
We're heading for Bar-Baral as we speak.
You can get anything there.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.130
Barba... cue?

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.840
Bar-Baral. It's a free city.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.350
Not even people like us
get a second glance there.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:53.680
It's a place where pirates from around
the world come to fence their booty.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.730
- Pirates?!
- Yep.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.730
An island of pirates...

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.940
Anyway, let's split up into teams.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.400
The one who's gonna stay behind
to guard the ship this time will be--

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.280
- Y-Yukimaru?
- Ah, there you are.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.660
Sorry to keep you waiting.
I was making this!

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:19.170
1         2         3         4         5         6         7
Ma     Shi      Karin     E     Kaede     Tsu     Yu

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:19.170
GO         STAY         GO         GO         GO         GO         GO
Tsubaki   Yukimaru   Kaede   Shitan   Makaba   Enju   Karin

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.840
Wow, left behind
five times in a row!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.380
Gotta hand it to Yukimaru!

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.760
Can you believe his luck?

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:28.180
Is it okay to leave him by himself?
Yukimaru seemed really depressed.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.300
Don't worry about him,
He's always like that.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.810
Why...?

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.280
There it is!

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.320
So that's Bar-Baral...

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:51.750
Free City "Bar-Baral"

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.330
Listen up! We're not here
for fun and games!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:59.290
Look, there's women in the harbor!
And they're all gorgeous!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.340
Going off on your own is prohibited!
Always remain focused on our objective!

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.340
- Who do you wanna hire?
- All of them! Every last one!

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.920
I'm talking about you two in particular!
Are you listening to me?!

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.340
I see, I see, aye aye sir!

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.090
Have all of you been here before?

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.600
Yes, aside from Karin.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.850
The food is first class.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.430
And one of us somehow manages
to never come ashore.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:33.030
- Now, where are the cute girls?
- Wow, look at that!

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.370
Okay, for now, let's make for
the center of the island.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.790
That's genuine <i>tamahagane</i> steel!

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.290
Everyone stay together.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.290
That goes double for you twins!
Got it?!

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.620
Yeah...

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:40.750
Prawns...

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.540
Is that-- It can't be!

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.750
Yakusugi cedar?!
Is it genuine? The real deal?

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:50.340
That's from a rhinoceros!
Rhino horn! Rhino! Rhino!

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:47.420
Clams...

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.930
Karin, dinner comes first.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.680
Nice catch, Makaba, but dinner
isn't our first order of business.

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:58.140
Rhino!

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.560
Hm? Where did Shitan go?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.560
You're so handsome
I'm about to melt into a puddle!

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.820
Come on up and stay a while.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.440
As much as I'd love to,
I have no money.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.910
For you, baby, it's on the house.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.910
Well, if you put it that way...

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.580
Shitan! Dinner comes first!

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:22.040
At the risk of repeating myself, Makaba,
dinner isn't the first order of business!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:26.800
Rhino! My rhino!
Don't go anywhere, you hear?!

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:27.590
Anyway, our group will stock up on medicines,
and the twins and Fena will see to provisions.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.340
Tsubaki, I hate to interrupt,

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:34.470
but those three haven't been
with us for a while now.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.060
Damn it...

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.310
Where did they go?!

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:49.030
So, what'll we have?
Pick anything you like, Fena!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.990
Um... Prawns and clams
and bread!

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:56.410
- Also, I'd like to try something exotic!
- Exotic?

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.740
Yeah! Something you can
only find here!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:02.210
I was right, everyone's staring at her.
It's that white hair...

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.080
- I don't know if there's anything like that here.
- There isn't?

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.580
I'll think of something.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.580
Fena, let's check out some clothing
stores before the restaurants.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.880
Dog. Are you familiar with
probabilities in <i>amidakuji?</i>

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.880
The odds are one in seven.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.800
With fewer horizontal lines,
you fall straight to the bottom.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.180
So if we call reaching
the bottom 100%,

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:02.310
by adding a line, that one in seven will move
left or right with a probability of six in seven.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:03.890
By taking the number
of lines and--

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:09.360
Damn it all...

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:12.900
Prawns!

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:13.820
Meat!

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.360
Clams!

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.280
Cheers!

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.450
That was delicious!

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.790
Whew, I'm stuffed, I'm stuffed...

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.450
I'm about to explode!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.040
That really was good!

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.920
You can count on
Makaba's recommendations!

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.710
With food, anyway.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.810
Isn't this--

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:50.270
This looks like that stone.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:55.070
Excuse me, would you happen to know
where this was made?

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.360
Hm?

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.860
If I tell you, will you buy it?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.030
Talk about rude!

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.290
- If we buy it, will you tell us?
- How much is it?

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.330
It's written on the bottom.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:06.870
Whoa!

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.870
If you've got no money, get lost.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.290
- Enju!
- I'm Kaede.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:14.130
Forget it, we don't have
that kind of money on us.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.210
But this is the first
lead we've had!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.510
We have to at least learn
where it's from!

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.760
Well, I suppose I'm open
to haggling.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.770
One night should do it.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:36.650
I'll trade that stone
for one night with you.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.030
Wha--

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.660
Hey, now!

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.370
Enju!

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.750
Wh-What's the big idea?
You got a problem with that?!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.790
You've got it all wrong.
This is me haggling, pops.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.380
I was thinking we could
make a trade!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.880
What in the world?!
It made fire!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.210
Pretty cool, huh?

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.260
Amazing!

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:03.550
Just twist this until it clicks, and poof!
It's super easy to use!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.890
Isn't that--
- One of Prof. Karin's inventions.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.390
I want it... I have to have it!
Son, how much do you want for it?!

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.900
The stone and information on
where it came from. Also,

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:18.530
an apology to our captain
for insulting her.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.150
We'll trade you for those.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.160
All right, damn it!
You drive a hard bargain.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:30.040
That stone was crafted at a place
in Germany called Libar-Oberstein.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:35.130
It's chipped and cracked now, but rumor has it
that it was once owned by a royal family.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:41.170
- Well?
- It even <i>feels</i> similar.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.220
Okay! I know where
we're headed next!

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:47.430
Cap'n Fena, maybe we should
think this through a bit more.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:49.350
"Similar" isn't enough
to act on.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:51.060
But there's a chance!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:55.060
Us stumbling across this stone
can't be a coincidence.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.070
Ever-Leaderscone, was it?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.820
Ever-Leaderstein.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:05.070
No offense, Fena, but I think
that's just an ordinary rock.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.450
But my senses are tingling!

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:09.830
Isn't that just a hunch?

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.500
Maybe, I'll give you that.
But still!

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:17.500
This is vital information obtained by
the coolest twins in the whole world!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.050
Coolest twins...

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.880
...in the whole world?

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:22.720
Peppermint candy...

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:24.680
Paper detective sexy.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:26.510
Shall we go there?

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.470
By all means, let's shall!

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:33.020
After all, we'd be acting on info obtained
by the coolest twins in the world!

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.440
How could it possibly
be wrong?!

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.270
Thank you, Angie!

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.110
When you said you can make men
do your bidding if you flatter them,

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.070
you were totally right.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.570
Wow, we really are the coolest.
<i>I</i> always knew, but still.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.990
You can say that again!
<i>I</i> knew, but still.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.490
I feel a little guilty.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.120
- Oops!
- Ow!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.620
Why did you stop?

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.260
Hey.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:06.380
I finally found you, Marginal!

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.890
No way.
What's he doing here?

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:13.310
You're not getting away this time!
Say your prayers.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:15.600
Hey, I don't know
what your deal is,

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.060
...but talking tough while hiding
behind a wall of women? Really?

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.980
Turn around and walk away--

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.320
Hand over that girl.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.870
You don't want to die, do you?

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.330
Kill them!

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.880
Yukimaru! We're back!

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:50.430
Sorry we took so long.
Blame it on the twins.

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.930
Boy, that was fun!
I bought so much!

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.890
I'm stuffed.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:59.150
Are the twins inside?
They need a good talking-to.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.270
We had to carry their share.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.820
What are you talking about?

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:06.240
They ditched us in town,
just like last time!

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.530
So we got stuck buying all the stuff
they were supposed to get!

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.240
What about Fena?

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:14.040
- Fena?
- Huh? She isn't back yet?

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.450
We assumed she was
with the twins.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:20.210
She's probably goofing off somewhere.
She'll come back once she gets hun--

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.220
You're worrying too much...

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.220
Whoa! Hey, now!

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.730
Careful, Miss!
That's unladylike!

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:54.240
Any ideas? They're tougher
than I thought.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:56.910
Looks like we won't be able to
handle 'em unless we fight for real.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.200
- Besides...
- ...Fena's here.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.870
Enju! Kaede!

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.170
Fena! Stand back!

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.890
There's no way out for you
this time.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:15.180
Come over here
before you get hurt.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.190
Yukimaru?!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.200
Wha--?

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.410
He killed eight men
in as many seconds...

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.170
Fena! Run over to Yukimaru!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.920
Yukimaru! Keep Fena safe!

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.170
Yukimaru!

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:52.930
Wh-Who the hell are you?!

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.100
Fena, get away from here
and hide.

00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:58.310
Get back!

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:04.230
We have no interest in pointless bloodshed.
If you value your lives, walk away!

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.320
If you refuse, we'll cut
you down without mercy.

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.400
Don't mess with me, boy!

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.530
My apologies, but I'm not going
to pull my punches this time!

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.290
Ow!

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.080
You little--

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:28.250
Women with a slender waist and
big boobs are humanity's greatest treasure.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.090
I'm not about to kill one.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:31.970
Huh?

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.350
Let's grab a bite
to eat sometime!

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.820
Yukimaru! We've got this!

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.360
Get Fena out of here!

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:55.610
Bastard!

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.450
Get moving!

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.660
After them!
Don't let them get away!

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.330
Now then, shall we mop things up?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.170
By all means, let's shall!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.490
Yukima--

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.650
You're not gettin' away!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.990
Hannah.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.330
Did you miss?

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.620
I could swear I hit him...

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.370
Where are the others?

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:33.170
Beats me.
Getting wiped out, probably.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.590
Then why are you here?!
You ran from the fight?!

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:38.340
You don't expect me to fight
the likes of them, do you?

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.340
Say what?!

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:42.050
For one thing,

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:44.010
I'm pretty sure

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.220
those guys were
the Goblin Knights.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.770
Ow! Darn it, Yukimaru!
Be gentler!

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:57.780
I appreciate you saving me and all,
but you need to treat a lady more gently!

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:07.330
There's no sign of pursuit. The twins should
be able to handle their remaining forces.

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.790
I think we can relax
for now--

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:21.380
Er, um... I...

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.550
Oh! Did that hurt?
I'm sorry!

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.180
Your right hand is hurt,
so I thought I should treat it.

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:28.890
Can you come over here a second?
I have some medicinal herbs--

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.430
Don't worry about me.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:33.940
It only grazed me.
Pay it no mind.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:35.940
- But I--
- More importantly,

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:40.860
think about your actions!
Everyone is risking their lives for you.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.200
This rash behavior needs to stop.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:45.950
Sorry.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.120
Let's go.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:06.850
Alba Regina. And vice versa.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:11.600
The beginning and the end...

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.120
Fena's work?

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:32.000
She's overreacting.
It's just a scratch.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:37.080
She handled herself pretty well. Maybe she's
more clever than we gave her credit for.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:37.080
The punishment of you three nitwits
will now be meted out!

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:42.840
To satisfy you own appetites, you three
shirked your duties to go stuff your faces!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:42.010
Of course she's good at <i>something.</i>
It just means she's human.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.550
And what's worse, in addition to
endangering your shipmates,

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:51.020
for reasons unknown and without discussion,
you decided on our next destination!

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:49.470
I'm more concerned about
those lady pirates...

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.020
Hm? What about them?

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.810
- Aw, come on!
- Silence!

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:54.520
No backtalk!

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:55.810
Forget it. It's nothing.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:59.110
For the crimes above, I sentence
the three of you to flinging!

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.570
- Makaba! Do it!
- 'Kay.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.780
Hang on! Me too?
Wait, Makaba!

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.290
Fena...

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.290
Don't do it!

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.170
Let go of me,
you Sconne bastards!

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.590
This can't be happening! Please!
Give me another chance!

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.970
I won't fail you again!
I'm begging you!

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.180
Your services
are no longer required.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.810
You're kidding, right?
Hey now... Wait! Wait!

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:37.310
Not in the water!
Not the water! I'm afraid of the water!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.700
Do you have any idea
who you are?

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:54.700
Abel...

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:58.710
The night has only just begun.
